\begin{align*}
1988x_0^2 + bx_0 + 8891 &= 0 \\
8891x_0^2 + bx_0 + 1988 &= 0.
\end{align*}
We can eliminate $x_0$ by subtracting the first equation from the second:
\begin{align*}
(8891x_0^2 + bx_0 + 1988) - (1988x_0^2 + bx_0 + 8891) &= 0 \\
6903x_0^2 - 6903 &= 0 \\
x_0^2 &= 1 \\
x_0 &= \pm 1.
\end{align*}
Substituting $x_0 = 1$ into the first equation gives us:
\begin{align*}
1988(1)^2 + b(1) + 8891 &= 0 \\
b &= -10879.
\end{align*}
Substituting $x_0 = -1$ into the first equation gives us:
\begin{align*}
1988(-1)^2 + b(-1) + 8891 &= 0 \\
b &= -10879.
\end{align*}
Thus, the set of values for $b$ is $\boxed{-10879}$. </think> <answer> -10879 </answer>

